    "id": "project-40",
    "title": "Cache Memory Performance Analysis Tool Using Ripes Simulator",
    "abstract": "Cache memory plays a vital role in improving the performance of modern processors by reducing memory access time. This project presents a Cache Memory Performance Analysis Tool implemented using the Ripes simulator. The objective of this project is to study the effect of cache parameters such as cache size and cache organization on processor performance. By executing the same RISC‑V program under different cache configurations, parameters such as cache hits, cache misses, execution cycles, and CPI are observed and analyzed. The results demonstrate that increasing cache size and associativity significantly reduces cache misses and improves overall system performance. This project helps in understanding the importance of cache memory in computer architecture.",
